      "description": "Faculty Openings - DePauw University DePauw University Students Families Employees Alumni Search Academics Academics Develop the leadership skills, critical thinking and experience necessary to lead in today’s world. Our brilliant faculty and co-curricular liberal arts approach make this transformation possible. Discover More Majors & Minors College of Liberal Arts and Sciences The Creative School School of Business and Leadership The Institute of Music Honor Scholars & Fellow Programs Centers at DePauw Academic Resources Study Abroad Research Internships Outcomes Admission & Aid Admission & Aid Your college degree is a vital investment in your future. We partner with you and your family to ensure the accessibility of our extraordinary academic and residential programs. Discover More Apply Scholarships & Aid The DePauw Promise Plan Your Visit Contact Admission Admitted Students Campus Life Campus Life Experience college life in high definition on our very involved and interconnected campus. With over 100 clubs and organizations plus a continuous calendar of community activities, there is no shortage of opportunity to get involved. Discover More Activities and Organizations Performing Arts & Culture Diversity and Inclusion Living on Campus Spiritual Life Fraternity & Sorority Life Wellness Athletics About About DePauw Discover a transformative learning environment that empowers you to be influential; to make a tangible difference on a global scale. Here you won’t just earn an education, you’ll live it. Discover More Mission and Impact Initiatives President White Location History & Traditions Quick Facts Our Community Stories Capital Projects Button Menu Visit Apply Get Info Give Faculty Openings Academic Affairs Contact Academic Affairs Open Faculty Positions Academic Handbook Faculty Resources Faculty Development Grants and Research Faculty Governance University Offices Academic Affairs Open Faculty Positions Open Faculty and Academic Affairs Positions Founded in 1837, DePauw University is a selective, undergraduate, national liberal arts college of just over 1,900 students, with a separate Institute of Music . The University, which has an endowment of $730 million, is located in Greencastle, Indiana, a town of 10,000 people, within an hour’s drive of Indianapolis, Terre Haute and Bloomington. Among DePauw’s distinctive features are its innovative Honors and Fellows programs , a strong tradition of community service, a large internship program, numerous international education programs , and success in attracting a diverse student body. DePauw has exceptional programs for supporting its faculty , including pre-tenure leaves for new faculty members and short- and long-term internal funding for professional and curriculum development activities. In support of DePauw University's mission and values, we welcome applications from members of underrepresented groups. DePauw University is an Equal Opportunity Employer and all qualified applicants will receive consideration without regard to race, color, religion, gender, gender identity or expression, sexual orientation, national origin, disability, age, or veteran status or any other federal, state, or local protected class. Faculty Positions Department Position Status Field/Specialty Institute of Music Part-Time Assistant Professor Accepting Applications Bassoon Institute of Music Part-Time Assistant Professor Accepting Applications Clarinet Institute of Music Part-Time Assistant Professor Accepting Applications Dance Institute of Music Part-Time Assistant Professor Accepting Applications Music Education Institute of Music Part-Time Assistant Professor Accepting Applications Violin Review of applications will begin on the indicated date and continue until positions are filled. For further information about these positions, write to the chair or dean of the corresponding department or school. Visit the Human Resources website for more information on other employment opportunities and job benefits at DePauw. Access DePauw University's Annual Safety Report here . Institute of MusicPart-Time Assistant ProfessorAccepting Applications DePauw University DePauw University 204 E. Seminary Greencastle, Indiana 46135-0037 Phone (765) 658-4800 Academics Admission & Aid Campus Life Athletics About Strategic Plan Directories Library Events News Employment Moodle Workday Google Apps Schedule a visit © 2026 DePauw University. All rights reserved.  DePauw University admits students of any race, color, national and ethnic origin to all the rights, privileges, programs, and activities generally accorded or made available to students at the school. It does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, national and ethnic origin in administration of its educational policies, admissions policies, scholarship and loan programs, and athletic and other school-administered programs. Privacy Policy | Cookie Policy | Terms and Conditions | Notice at Collection | Your Privacy Choices | Non-Discrimination Policy | Title IX"
